A||||5||Cooter||Fiero vs. Explorer||||8
Z||000000||Cooter||10-10-1999||12:04 PM||||My morning drive is on a 2 lane rural road with a 45 mph speed limit. I usually run about 50-55 mph because there is not much traffic. Some kid gets behind me in a late model Explorer and is tail-gateing me really bad. The speed limit drops to 35 and so do I. That sudden braking made him mad, so he got even closer. He was so busy watching me that he did not realize the road makes a 15 mph 90 degree turn. I downshifted the Fiero and took the curve at 35. I heard a lot of tire sliding noises and saw the Explorer slid off the road and through the grass before smacking a curb with right front tire. It did not look too serious, just a flat tire and bent wheel. Maybe this will teach him his lesson about sharp curves in SUV's. Fiero- 1, Explorer-0||||reg||8
Z||000001||GT Bastard||10-10-1999||01:44 PM||||Damn, that's pretty hard-core!!! That'll teach him to try and hang wit da big dogs.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Eric||10-10-1999||07:40 PM||||That's funny as hell!  I've tried that a few times with no luck.  I guess you just have to hope for a stupid bastard in a non-turning car who doesn't know his way around.||||reg||10
Z||000003||batboy||10-10-1999||09:07 PM||||Yippee! A tailgater got what they deserved. What is it with all these stupid tailgaters? They are getting worse and worse all the time. When I'm driving my ratty ol' Suburban, I usually stomp on the brakes hoping they'll hit me so I can collect some insurance, but I don't dare do that in any of my Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||10-10-1999||10:53 PM||||Poor geek,probably thought it was a video game;all you have to do is turn the wheel right?<BR>A good one for people passing at high speeds in low speed limit areas is to move left,then back,brake hard;usually they exit stage left.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||10-11-1999||12:09 AM||||I was with a friend in his car  the other day when some old lady in her caddy was tailgating us badly.  I thought she would hit us. He hit those windshield washer jets, had to let off when he ran out of fluid(there was plenty when he started spraying) she ended up passing us in the left turn only lane, giving us the "universal symbol". We were just laughing and grinning when we noticed she had just purchased the BRAND NEW Caddilac earlier that day.(temp tag said so)  Maybe next time she'll think twice next time she decides to tailgate bored college students.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-11-1999).]||||reg||1
